From 15a2fd94578adf0b5404b1b561e1287667c8da08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 22:20:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(automations): Promote winners into multiple target ad
 sets

The Promote action could only duplicate a winning ad into a single
target ad set. This lets a rule fan a winner out to several ad sets
across as many campaigns as you like.

- AdSetSearch gains an optional `multiple` mode with chips + toggle
  selection (mirrors CampaignSearch); single-select stays the default
  so the trigger's ad-set filter is unchanged.
- Promote action UI uses the multi-select picker; target_adset_id /
  target_adset_name are stored comma-separated (backward compatible
  with a single ID).
- Evaluate route duplicates the winner into each target ad set,
  tolerates partial failures, and only pauses the original once at
  least one duplication succeeds.
- Slack notification reflects the multi-target count.
- Added i18n keys across all locales and config round-trip tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WCxaTyJA2qcWAfA8gzxMyY
